### Health

GET {{PlantCare_Api_HostAddress}}/health
Accept: text/plain


### System status

GET {{PlantCare_Api_HostAddress}}/api/system/status
Accept: application/json


### Current authenticated user
### Run this first to verify that AccessToken works.

GET {{PlantCare_Api_HostAddress}}/api/account/me
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{AccessToken}}


### Create a Monstera species

POST {{PlantCare_Api_HostAddress}}/api/plant-species
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{AccessToken}}

{
  "commonName": "Monstera",
  "scientificName": "Monstera deliciosa",
  "description": "A tropical climbing plant known for its split leaves.",
  "sunlightRequirement": "BrightIndirectLight",
  "sunlightInstructions": "Place near a bright window without prolonged direct sunlight.",
  "defaultWateringIntervalDays": 7,
  "wateringInstructions": "Water when the top layer of soil feels dry.",
  "defaultFertilizingIntervalDays": 30,
  "fertilizingInstructions": "Fertilize monthly during spring and summer.",
  "soilInstructions": "Use a loose, nutrient-rich and well-draining potting mixture.",
  "humidityInstructions": "Prefers moderate to high humidity.",
  "minimumTemperatureCelsius": 18,
  "maximumTemperatureCelsius": 30,
  "isToxicToPets": true
}


### Create an Aloe species

POST {{PlantCare_Api_HostAddress}}/api/plant-species
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{AccessToken}}

{
  "commonName": "Aloe Vera",
  "scientificName": "Aloe vera",
  "description": "A popular, fleshy-leaved succulent known for its medicinal soothing gel and rosette growth habit.",
  "sunlightRequirement": "FullSun",
  "sunlightInstructions": "Requires six to eight hours of direct sunlight daily for robust growth.",
  "defaultWateringIntervalDays": 14,
  "wateringInstructions": "Water deeply only when the potting soil is completely dry.",
  "defaultFertilizingIntervalDays": 60,
  "fertilizingInstructions": "Apply a diluted succulent fertilizer once every two months during spring and summer.",
  "soilInstructions": "Use a gritty, well-draining cactus and succulent commercial potting blend.",
  "humidityInstructions": "Thrives in low humidity environments and tolerates dry indoor air.",
  "minimumTemperatureCelsius": 10,
  "maximumTemperatureCelsius": 29,
  "isToxicToPets": true
}


### Get the complete plant catalog

GET {{PlantCare_Api_HostAddress}}/api/plant-species
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{AccessToken}}


### Get one plant species

GET {{PlantCare_Api_HostAddress}}/api/plant-species/{{PlantSpeciesId}}
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{AccessToken}}


### Current user WITHOUT authentication
### This should return 401 if /api/account/me requires authorization.

GET {{PlantCare_Api_HostAddress}}/api/account/me
Accept: application/json


### Register another test user

POST {{PlantCare_Api_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "nico@example3.com",
  "password": "PlantCare2026!"
}


### Login using token mode
### Use this request whenever you need fresh access/refresh tokens.

POST {{PlantCare_Api_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login?useCookies=false
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "nico@example2.com",
  "password": "PlantCare2026!"
}


### Invalid login
### This should return 401.

POST {{PlantCare_Api_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login?useCookies=false
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "nico@example2.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword123"
}


### Refresh authentication tokens
### Copy the NEW accessToken and refreshToken from the response
### back into the variables at the top of this file.

POST {{PlantCare_Api_HostAddress}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{RefreshToken}}"
}


### Get antiforgery token

GET {{PlantCare_Api_HostAddress}}/api/antiforgery/token
Accept: application/json


### Get my plants

GET {{PlantCare_Api_HostAddress}}/api/my-plants
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{AccessToken}}